Source: dracut-luks
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Joshua Miller <freshroot@lamille.net>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2

Package: dracut-luks
Architecture: all
Depends: dracut, cryptsetup, grub2-common, util-linux, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: lvm2, tpm2-tools
Suggests: libfido2-1
Description: dracut configuration for unlocking a LUKS root at boot
 Installs alongside dracut on Ubuntu and makes an encrypted root boot
 without hand-editing the kernel command line.
 .
 A /etc/default/grub.d drop-in derives the LUKS container of / at
 update-grub time and appends the matching dracut unlock parameters
 (rd.luks.uuid, rd.luks.name, and rd.lvm.vg when LVM sits between LUKS
 and the root device). Because the values are resolved on every
 update-grub rather than baked in, re-encrypting or cloning the disk
 does not leave a stale command line behind.
 .
 A dracut.conf.d drop-in pulls the crypt modules into every initramfs,
 and a second one adds FIDO2 and TPM2 token support when the
 corresponding libraries are installed. Tokens enrolled in the LUKS2
 header (systemd-cryptenroll) are detected at update-grub time and the
 matching tpm2-device=auto / fido2-device=auto options emitted via
 rd.luks.options, so hardware-token unlock works without further
 configuration. TPM2 support in the initramfs needs tpm2-tools
 installed (see Recommends).
 .
 The dracut-luks-setup helper reports what the drop-ins resolve to,
 adds a missing /etc/crypttab entry, preserves the initramfs-tools
 images before dracut replaces them, and verifies the result.
 .
 This package concerns itself only with unlocking the root volume. It
 does not create LUKS containers, enroll keys, or manage fstab.
